@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@
+# smallpt browser studio
+
+Kevin Beason’s original C++ smallpt integrator, compiled to WebAssembly using Emscripten. Open `index.html` through an existing static host. All path tracing runs locally in a dedicated module Web Worker; no backend, GPU API, shared memory, or cross-origin isolation headers are required.
+
+The page starts a render automatically. Use **Randomize & render** for new sphere colors, or choose colors, resolution, and sample count and press **Render scene**. Rendering can be stopped; the download control saves the current canvas as PNG.
+
+## Build
+
+Requires Node.js and Emscripten (`em++` on PATH).
+
+```sh
+npm run build
+```
+
+This compiles `src/renderer.cpp` into `assets/smallpt.js` and `assets/smallpt.wasm`, then packages the static page in `dist/`. Compiled assets are included so the page also works without rebuilding. Serve `.wasm` with the `application/wasm` content type where possible (the Emscripten loader supports an ArrayBuffer fallback).
+
+To validate the actual Wasm module and regenerate the initial 256-sample preview without a browser or server:
+
+```sh
+node scripts/render-preview.mjs
+npm run build
+```
+
+The check exercises the generated ES module and Wasm, checks deterministic rendering and sphere color changes, and writes `assets/preview.png` using output from that same module. The preview provides an initial image while the live render starts. No stock or AI-generated imagery is used.
+
+## Source and license
+
+Original source: https://www.kevinbeason.com/smallpt/
+
+`vendor/smallpt/smallpt.cpp` is the upstream 99-line source, retained unchanged, along with Kevin Beason’s MIT license. `src/renderer.cpp` replaces only the command-line render loop with a scanline API and adds sphere color controls. The original recursive radiance integrator, scene geometry, materials, antialiasing, gamma correction, and ray intersections are retained. OpenMP is omitted: the browser uses a Web Worker instead. The build disables C++ exceptions and accepts the original 2008 source’s implicit integer narrowing.
